{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Eliav ben Cheilon.</b> He is called so because that which establishes Issachar to learn Torah is called a father, and as we find that Moses placed [Zebulun] before Issachar, as it is written (Deuteronomy 33:18): ״שְׂמַח זְבוּלֻן וְגוֹ׳ וְיִשָּׂשכָר״ וְגוֹ׳. And this is the meaning of <b>Eliav</b>: to me he will be accounted to be called a father, even though he is <b>Cheilon</b>, meaning profane — that he is not a son of Torah and deals in the commerce of this profane world; even so, he is a father to the king."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:34.269011592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}